# ============================================================
#  AI E-LEARNING PLATFORM — CURSOR RULES
# ============================================================

## IDENTITY
Django 5 + DRF backend. React 18 + Vite frontend.
Auth: JWT access token in memory + refresh in httpOnly cookie.
Database: SQLite (dev) → PostgreSQL (prod).

## FILE LOCATIONS (never deviate)
models.py · serializers.py · views.py · urls.py · tasks.py
permissions.py · signals.py · apps.py · admin.py
src/api/ · src/context/ · src/shared/ · src/student/ · src/admin/ · src/store/

## BACKEND — MANDATORY PATTERNS
- Always define __str__, Meta(ordering, verbose_name) on every model
- Use db_index=True on every FK used in filter/join
- unique_together in Meta — never rely on application logic
- Serializers: always ModelSerializer, never fields="__all__"
- Views: always ViewSets via DefaultRouter; explicit permission_classes on every view
- ORM: select_related() for FK, prefetch_related() for reverse FK
- Celery: @shared_task only; import models inside task function, not at module level
- Permissions: role field only — never is_staff or is_superuser

## FRONTEND — MANDATORY PATTERNS
- ALL HTTP calls through src/api/*.js — never fetch/axios in components
- All server state via React Query (useQuery/useMutation)
- Quiz session state via Zustand (src/store/quizStore.js only)
- No inline styles except dynamic values — Tailwind classes only
- Protected routes via AuthGuard; admin routes via RoleGuard — never check roles in pages

## NAMING CONVENTIONS
Django: PascalCase models, ModelSerializer, ModelViewSet, snake_case tasks
React: PascalCase components/pages, useCamelCase hooks, camelCase api functions

## WHAT CURSOR MUST NEVER DO
- Raw SQL (cursor.execute)
- localStorage/sessionStorage for tokens
- fields = "__all__" in serializers
- Import Celery app in tasks — use @shared_task
- Write CSS files — Tailwind only
- Add unapproved packages silently
- Put business logic in views — use service functions or tasks
- Call axios/fetch directly in components

## APPROVED PACKAGES
Backend: django, djangorestframework, djangorestframework-simplejwt,
  celery, redis, django-cors-headers, dj-database-url,
  requests, beautifulsoup4, spacy, youtube-transcript-api,
  django-ratelimit, argon2-cffi, psycopg2-binary, python-decouple
Frontend: react, react-dom, react-router-dom, @tanstack/react-query,
  axios, recharts, zustand, react-hot-toast, vite

## SCOPE GUARD
If a request would add a new model, new package, new route, or
architectural change not in the existing plan — respond:
"This is outside current MVP scope. Confirm before proceeding."
Do not silently expand scope.

## PROMPT FORMAT — HOW TO GET BEST RESULTS
Every prompt must state:
1. Target file path
2. Current state ("does not exist" or "already has X — do not modify")
3. Specific class/function/component name
4. Inputs and outputs (request body → response shape, or props → rendered output)
5. One rule from these rules that applies